essed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"KIF5B","as_reported":"c.1493 T > C (p.Leu498Pro)","cdna":"c.1493T>C","protein":"p.Leu498Pro","genomic":"","zygosity":"heterozygous","origin":"de_novo","consequence":"missense","key":"V6"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"de novo","inheritance":"AD","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Subject 3 (p.Leu498Pro) was a 6-year-old female with mild DD, severe hypotonia, swallowing and feeding difficulties since infancy requiring G-tube feeding for the first 7 months of life, and recurrent vomiting.","Subject 3 (p.Leu498Pro) was affected by a multisystemic hypotonic condition starting since the prenatal period with decreased fetal movements.","variant validation and co-segregation analyses confirmed either the de novo origin of the variant (subject 3) or its co-segregation with the trait (family 2)"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AD","genotype_reason":"heterozygous de novo variant"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:36018820:1","pmid":"36018820","section":"animal_model","statement":"Flex et al. (2023) injected mRNA encoding the KIF5B-related kyphomelic dysplasia variant p.Thr195Lys into zebrafish embryos and observed heart size and morphology defects with cardiac edema at 2 dpf, a wider ceratohyal cartilage angle at 3 dpf, and reduced mitochondrial coverage along motoneuron axons, consistent with a dominant (possibly dominant-negative) effect.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["the c.584C > A missense substitution (p.Thr195Lys), the latter as representative of the pathogenic variants identified in individuals presenting with KIF5B-related KD","Overexpression of KIF5BThr195Lys and KIF5BAsn255del resulted in a wide range of morphological defects in heart size and anatomy, which were scored as mild or severe, and embryos expressing these variants presented heart oedemas at 2 dpf","the ceratohyal cartilage angle was less acute in all of the embryos injected with mutant KIF5B variants compared to those expressing the WT protein or non-injected embryos"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:36018820:2","pmid":"36018820","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Flex et al. (2023) noted on structural modeling that the 3 missense variants previously implicated in KIF5B-related kyphomelic dysplasia (affecting Lys91, Thr195, and Gly234) map to the motor domain and cluster in the pocket mediating ATP/ADP binding.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["three recently reported missense variants implicated in KIF5B-related KD affected residues (Lys91, Thr195 and Gly234) also mapping at the motor domain, clustering in the pocket mediating ATP/ADP binding"],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:36018820:3","pmid":"36018820","section":"genotype_phenotype_correlations","statement":"Reviewing their patients together with the 4 previously reported KIF5B-related kyphomelic dysplasia patients, Flex et al. (2023) found that joint contractures/clubfoot occurred only in subjects with variants in the kinesin motor domain, and proposed grouping the phenotypes, which share hypotonia, DD/ID, and a suggestive facial gestalt, as KIF5B-related diseases.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["joint contractures were observed only in subjects carrying pathogenic variants within the kinesin motor domain (p.Asn255del, family 2 of the present series; p.Lys91Arg, p.Thr195Lys and p.Gly234Val, from Itai’s series).","So we anticipate DD/ID, hypotonia, and a suggestive facial gestalt as recurrent features of this new class of disorders regardless any other associated signs","we propose to group them as KIF5B-related diseases"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:36018820:4","pmid":"36018820","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Flex et al. (2023) found that patient fibroblasts heterozygous for KIF5B variants showed aberrant primary cilia, enlarged and peripherally distributed lysosomes, perinuclear enlarged autophagosomes, Golgi disorganization, and misoriented microtubule growth, and proposed altered microtubule dynamics as the unifying event.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["The analysis performed in starved fibroblasts revealed the presence of aberrant primary cilium formation in all patients’ cell lines","showed a marked increase in the size and number of lysosomes, which also display an anomalous distribution that was particularly enriched at the cell periphery","these findings identified an altered MT dynamics and organization as a unifying event in primary cells from the subjects with KIF5B variants causing aberrant vesicular distribution"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:36018820:5","pmid":"36018820","section":"clinical_management","statement":"Flex et al. (2023) recommended cardiac surveillance in all individuals with KIF5B variants because late-onset dilated cardiomyopathy could not be excluded in younger patients.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["we cannot exclude possible late-onset DCM in them. Cardiac surveillance is highly recommended in all these subjects."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:35342932:1","pmid":"35342932","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"In 4 individuals with kyphomelic dysplasia, Itai et al. (2022) identified de novo heterozygous variants in the KIF5B gene by whole-exome sequencing. All variants affected conserved amino acids in or close to the ATPase activity-related motifs in the catalytic motor domain of KIF5B.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["We performed whole-exome sequencing and evaluated the pathogenicity of the identified variants.","All variants involved conserved amino acids in or close to the ATPase activity-related motifs in the catalytic motor domain of the KIF5B protein."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:35342932:2","pmid":"35342932","section":"description","statement":"Itai et al. (2022) described kyphomelic dysplasia as a heterogeneous group of skeletal dysplasias with severe limb bowing and variable findings such as narrow thorax and abnormal facies, and suggested that heterozygous KIF5B variants cause a specific form, extending the phenotypic spectrum of kinesinopathies.","inheritance":"AD","quotes":["Kyphomelic dysplasia is a heterogeneous group of skeletal dysplasias characterized by severe bowing of the limbs associated with other variable findings, such as narrow thorax and abnormal facies.","Our findings suggest that heterozygous KIF5B deleterious variants cause a specific form of kyphomelic dysplasia."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["KIF5B"],"confirmed":["KIF5B"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AD"]}